WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.540
Before we start talking about the Slavic migration
in to Balkans during the 5th and 6th century

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.770
we have to look at the area prior to their
arrival.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.080
Most of the Balkans have always been kind
of poorly settled due to its mountains and

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.290
thick forests.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.380
The cities and towns that did exist where
either by major in land routes or the sea.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:21.430
The towns below this line were largely greek
where as the towns above it had more mixed

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.430
population.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.320
For example the towns near the see where very
much Latin as oppose to the towns which were

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.320
more inland.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.080
These probably still spoke Latin as it was
the mane trading language in the area but

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.550
they were mostly made up of Illyrian, Thracian,
Dacian and the remnants of some Germanic tribes.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.449
However when the area came under the control
of the Byzantines even the northern cities

00:00:40.449 --> 00:00:41.710
started to get more hellenized.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.649
Now that we covered the cities let's look
at the countryside, what little of it was

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:50.139
populated, was mostly either by the descendants
of retired Roman soldiers which often times

00:00:50.139 --> 00:00:54.949
at the end of their service where given land
in the Balkan region and or Illyrians, thracians,

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:58.872
Dacians, greeks and again some remnantses
of Germanic tribes (Gepids, Goths, OstroGoths

00:00:58.872 --> 00:00:59.872
etc.).

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:03.280
And even though this may seem like a lot of
people, numbers wise it truly wasn’t.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.960
There was also no clear predominant division
between these farming settlements, it would

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.390
be completely common to find a valley with
illyrian farmers next to a valley of Germanic

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.380
farmers next to two more valleys that were
not settled.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.950
It is also reasonable to assume that all these
people intermingled in one way or another,

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.520
creating a small but diverse population.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.030
Furthermore the reason why the Balkans were
so poorly settled and had a low economic development

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.750
was because of its Geography.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.850
As mentioned before due to its mountains and
forested nature of the area and its location

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:36.060
right next to the Pannonian plain meant that
many nomadic tribes could easily raid in to

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.320
the region and then quickly retreat before
any kind of defence could be mounted as it

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.289
took a long time to transport troops in the
region.

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:46.539
Now that we have a small understanding of
the area let’s look at the Slavic migration

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.710
in to the Balkans.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:52.460
Prior to their maine arrival in the 6th century
the Balkans suffered major raids from Germanic

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.619
and Hunnic tribes.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:58.149
We have written records stating that small
towns where abandoned roads were destroyed

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:00.729
and the large chunk of the population fled.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:04.899
The remaining people in the area lived in
sizeable fortified towns which were mostly

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:06.729
left alone during the raids.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:10.800
It is possible that some Slavs came to the
Balkans with these Germanic and Hunnic tribes

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.250
as early as the 3rd century but even with
that it would be a very small percentage.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.610
The main wave of the slavs came during the
6th century continuing in to the 7th.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.590
The migration went either through the Lower
Danube Region however due to a more direct

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:28.280
Byzantine control of that area and the fact
it was more populated as it was largely spared

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.100
during the radingin period meant that this
wasn’t a popular spot of crossing for the

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.100
Slavs.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.560
That is why the majority of the slavic tribes
went through the Moravian and Zemplin passes

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.750
in to the Pannonian basin and then into the
Balkans.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.840
Now it is important to understand that this
slavic migration didn’t happen at ones.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.510
It was more than a century long affair of
migration with intertwined larger and smaller

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.880
waves of settlers coming in to the region.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.630
So why Didn’t the Byzantines stop the slavs?

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.171
Well there are multiple reasons why the Byzantine
didn’t protect the Balkans from the slavic

00:02:57.171 --> 00:03:00.260
settlers even though it was under their control.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.370
First it was because the slavs left the towns
and cities alone settling in the countryside

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:08.430
that wasn’t either populated in the first
place or was abandoned due to the raids.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:12.650
This happened on a such a large scale that
Procopius and other writers mentioned that

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.120
the cities in the Balkans where like islands
in a slavic see.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:20.120
So to the Byzantines there was nothing really
to protect since the slavs where taking up

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.480
area that was empty in the first place.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.220
This also meant that some Byzantines were
happy with the slavs as they were rebuilding

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.400
and resetting the area that was destroyed
before.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.750
Second reason why the Byzantense didn’t
stop the slavs was because during much of

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.700
the early slavic migration Justinian was busy
requiring italy.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:41.730
And even if they had some free armies to fight
the slavs, Procopius writes that it was almost

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.570
impossible as if the “Byzantines defeated
or made a pact with one tribe, that arrangement

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:51.260
was valid for just one small group and had
no effect on any other tribe”.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:55.120
This slavic disunity can be seen in the various
ways they settled the Balkans.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.460
The first wave of the Slavs were “mostly”
peaceful settlers minding to their own business

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.760
but after them in the 560s Slavic tribes living
outside of the Byzantine empire held frequent

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.600
yearly raids that went as far as northern
Greece.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.200
And since there where already some Slavs living
in the Balkans it was obviuse that many Slavic

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.970
tribes didn’t care much for each other fighting
between themselves as often as fighting against

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:17.970
others.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:22.780
These yearly raids culminated during 570s
and 80s when the Avars came to central Europe

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.440
and started to solidify their rule over the
slavic tribes in the area.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.880
As such the slavs that where still living
on the Border with the Byzantine Empire held

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.650
much larger raids in to the Balkans then before.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.350
We have an account of one of these raids by
John of Ephesus but we know there where more

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.970
raids then just the one.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.500
These raids were different then the ones prior
to this.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.320
First because they were much larger involving
100k people and second after the radining

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.360
stopped instead of going back to the Avar
control territory the Slavs just stayed in

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.360
the Balkans.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.060
The Avars not wanting to be left out from
all the radining also started to raid the

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.200
Balkans including the newly settled Slavs.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.889
All of this was possible at the time because
the Byzantine army was fighting the Persians

00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:01.889
in the East.

00:05:01.889 --> 00:05:04.530
There where basically no soldiers left to
protect the Western Regions.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:10.070
When the Persian war ended in 591, Emperor
Maurice finally could address the the Avar

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.310
and Slavic problem.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.810
In the year 600 he managed to drove out the
Avars along with some of the Slavs but majority

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.900
of them have already settled in to a farming
life in the area.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.560
At this point numbering hundreds of thousands
if not millions.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.080
And even though the Byzantines tried the age
old Roman tactic of resettling tribes throughout

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.990
the empire sending some Slavs to Anatolia
and even the Caucuses it didn’t prove effective

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:36.810
as these where small numbers compared to the
actual Slavic population of the Balkans at

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.810
this point.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.620
During the 7th century as the wars between
the Avars and Byzantines continued.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.690
So did the constant flow of Slavic people
fleeing the Avar Khaganate and settling in

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:46.860
to the Balkans.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.260
The North now being almost completely Slavic
and the South starting to get more and more

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:52.260
settlements.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.919
There where even some accounts of Slavs trying
to raid and settle Greek Islands.

00:05:55.919 --> 00:06:00.310
It was also during this time that many cities
and towns which held out like islands to Slavic

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.000
assimilations started to be slowly quote unquote
converted.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.350
Now it is important to note that even though
some of these towns were military conquered

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:13.270
most of them were just peacefully assimilated
over time into the much larger Slavic population.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.880
It is also important to recognise that during
this time there was lots of fighting and power

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.230
grabbing in the Balkans.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.540
So even though the recognised area of Byzantine
control was this, there were lots of autonomous

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:26.940
areas some of which still saw themselves as
part of the Empire some which didn’t, some

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:31.330
of which were subdued by the Byzantines some
of which were not and then add the Avars for

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.160
even more complications.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.850
So the Balkans where in this constant flux
of uncertain political control by various

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:38.850
groups.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.200
But by far the Byzantines usually ended up
having the upper hand in the end.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:46.820
The Balkans now almost completely settled
by the Slavs formed a dialect continuum.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:50.400
This means that even though we are certain
the numerous slavic tribes had many different

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.770
dialects they still could understand each
other.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.710
And even though this continuum still exist
in a different form to this day there are

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.370
clear differences from the one now to the
one in the early 7th century.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.990
One of these changes to this continuum was
the arrival of the Croats and Serbs.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:09.620
They arrived around the early to middle 7th
century to find numerous slavic tribes already

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:10.920
living in the Balkans.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.250
Where the Croats and Serbs came from is very
much still debated.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:18.110
We know for sure they came from the lands
north of the Danube as this is where all the

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:22.300
Slavs in the Balkans came from however the
specifics of why they decided to come to the

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:27.500
Balkans and how they manage to become so prominent
in a see of many different slavic tribes is

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.090
still largely unknown.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:33.290
The likeliest origin is that the Serbs and
Croats just as many other slavic tribes where

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.889
under the Avar control going in to the 7th
century.

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:40.090
They then used the commotion and the Khaganate’s
instability during the Samo’s independence

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:43.400
war to migrate in to a more favorable area
in the Balkans.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:47.070
This theory is supported by the fact that
the formation of Samo’s Kingdom correlates

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.340
with the dates of our presumed understanding
of Serbian and Croatian arrival in to the

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.340
Balkans.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:57.090
It is also very much possible that this wasn’t
just a single one off migration by these two

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:02.240
groups and the trickle of Serbian and Croatian
people continued in to the 8th and 9th century.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.980
Ones the two tribes established themselves
they quickly started influence the people

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:10.320
around them which can been seen today by the
fact that the people in the area speak a variation

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.410
of the Serbo-Croatian language.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:17.180
Also during this time some of the people in
this area migrated North West in to today's

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.180
Slovenia.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.460
Here they found western Slavic tribes from
Moravia which came to the area during the

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.340
first Slavic wave in the 6th century, however
more waves may have occurred all the way till

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.919
the fall of Samo’s Empire.

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:31.830
This mix of slavic tribes resulted in a unique
Slovenian culture and language which today

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:34.860
isn’t either western slavic nor Serbo-Croatian.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:41.330
This area was at start controlled by the Byzantines
then conquered by the Avars and briefly vsaalized

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.330
by Samo’s Kingdom.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.810
But when Samo died large part of the area
fell back to the Avars.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:49.980
Nonetheless a small county Carantania manage
to remain independent partly due to the natural

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.889
mountains protection and partly due to the
Frankish influence in the area.

00:08:53.889 --> 00:08:58.970
Then in 745 being threatened by the Avars
and most likely pressured by the Bavarians

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.519
the county first became part of Bavaria and
then annexed by the Carolingian Empire along

00:09:03.519 --> 00:09:07.089
with the lands lost to the Avars after the
death of Samo.

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:11.740
During the 8th century Byzantines, Croats,
Serbs and Avars all had some sort of a political

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.589
power match within today’s Serbo-Croatian
area.

00:09:14.589 --> 00:09:19.279
However due to unreliable and sparse written
records there’s nothing we can say for certain

00:09:19.279 --> 00:09:20.999
about this area during this time.

00:09:20.999 --> 00:09:25.559
It is most likely that during this struggle
the Serbs and Croats established some political

00:09:25.559 --> 00:09:29.009
autonomy but the extend of that autonomy is
unknown.

00:09:29.009 --> 00:09:33.029
Nevertheless we can presume that the Serbian
Vlastimirovic dynasty was established and

00:09:33.029 --> 00:09:37.470
the precursors to the Croatian duchies of
Pannonia and Dalmatia may have started to

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.509
form shape.

00:09:38.509 --> 00:09:42.230
Although this wouldn’t have been actual
duchies as feudalism still wasn’t in the

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:43.230
area.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:46.860
They would have been more of a coalition of
tribes trying to fight for autonomy against

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.940
the Avars, Byzantine and other surrounding
tribes.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:53.490
But while all of this was happening there
was another group which shaped south slavic

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.899
history and one we have more reliable sources
about.

00:09:56.899 --> 00:10:02.319
The Bulgars where a coalition of nomadic Turkic
tribes originating somweher from Central Asia.

00:10:02.319 --> 00:10:06.980
Over time this group also absorbed some Iranian,
Hunnic and other Indo-European people but

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:09.699
their lifestyle remained very much nomadic.

00:10:09.699 --> 00:10:13.660
During the early 7th century they inhabited
the area of today’s Eastern Ukraine but

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.990
where under the control of the Avars.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.279
That all started to change when the Avars
and Sassanids made an anti Byzantine alliance.

00:10:20.279 --> 00:10:24.420
The Romans feeling threatened quickly started
to look for allies of their own.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:28.499
They made friends with the powerful Bulgar
Dulo clan and as a sign of friendship the

00:10:28.499 --> 00:10:31.389
clan send some of its children to the Byzantine
court.

00:10:31.389 --> 00:10:36.519
One of these children was Kubrat who was said
to be a quick learner and had great admirations

00:10:36.519 --> 00:10:37.519
for the Byzantines.

00:10:37.519 --> 00:10:42.029
While at the Roman court Kubrat was said to
have converted to christianity before returning

00:10:42.029 --> 00:10:43.370
back home.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:47.129
Ones Kubrat returned he used what he learned
from the Romans and manage to unite the other

00:10:47.129 --> 00:10:51.339
Bulgar tribes under one banner, promising
to free them from the Avars.

00:10:51.339 --> 00:10:55.939
Then presumably during the Byzantine Sassanid
war when Avars where busy raiding the Balkans

00:10:55.939 --> 00:10:58.059
Kubrat rebelled and won.

00:10:58.059 --> 00:11:01.939
Quickly after this victory he solidified his
power and became the ruler of what we call

00:11:01.939 --> 00:11:03.860
Great Bulgaria.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:08.389
Continuing on Great Bulgaria and the Byzantines
had a close relationship and Kubrat’s reign

00:11:08.389 --> 00:11:10.870
was very prosperous for the Bulgarian people.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:16.009
He eventually died around 650s and 60s leaving
the kingdom to his sons.

00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:19.999
With their distrust of each other combined
with the Kazar aggression the brothers divided

00:11:19.999 --> 00:11:24.050
up the Kingdom and lead their people to settle
different areas within Europe.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:28.459
One of these brothers Asparuh who traveled
along the Black Sea quickly came in to a dispute

00:11:28.459 --> 00:11:29.800
with the Byzantines.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:34.129
After a few battles the most decisive one
being the battle of Ongal he manage to win

00:11:34.129 --> 00:11:39.740
and settle the area of Lower Danube in 681
which is regarded as the foundation year of

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.170
modern Bulgaria.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:45.619
Few years later another brother of Asparuh,
Kuber who first went to the Pannonian plain

00:11:45.619 --> 00:11:51.490
and became an Avar vassal rebelled and migrated
with his people to an area of modern day Macedonia.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:56.380
Here after few battles he became a Byzantine
vassal around the end of 680s and this is

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:01.610
where all written records about Kuber and
his people end, presumably settling and assimilating

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.310
into the local population.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:06.160
This population being overwhelmingly slavic.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.439
In fact the slavic population in the lands
settled by the Bulgars was so numerous that

00:12:10.439 --> 00:12:15.350
after just 2 centuries the Bulgar language
died off and what remains to this day is a

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.429
Bulgaro-Macedonian slavic language.

00:12:17.429 --> 00:12:22.309
What the Bulgars manage to achieve in the
next 2 centuries is impressive and could easily

00:12:22.309 --> 00:12:23.620
have its own video.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:28.339
In a very brief way they established the First
Bulgar Empire and even though it had some

00:12:28.339 --> 00:12:33.790
setbacks on occasion with some internal strife
they managed to expand in to much of Southeastern

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.559
Europe by the 9th century.

00:12:35.559 --> 00:12:40.269
They accomplished this through carefully crafted
diplomatic actions, numerous military victories

00:12:40.269 --> 00:12:42.970
and expansion in to the former Avar territory.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.989
This meant that Bulgaria stretched from the
Black Sea to Pest from the Dniester to the

00:12:46.989 --> 00:12:48.350
Ionian Sea.

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:49.980
But bulgaria had a problem.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.819
It was still pagan in an increasingly Christianised
world.

00:12:53.819 --> 00:12:57.910
Boris the 1st new that converting would result
in far better diplomatic relations but he

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:01.910
was already afraid of the increasing Byzantine
influence in his realm.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:06.490
So his first idea was to convert to Roman
Catholicism rather than Eastern Orthodox.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:12.690
However this brief flirt with Catholicism
didn’t last because in 864 Boris lost a

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:17.070
war with the Byzantines and in the peace treaty
agreed to convert to Eastern Orthodox along

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.509
with his people.

00:13:18.509 --> 00:13:22.309
Naturally no one was happy as Boris didn’t
want the increase byzantine influence over

00:13:22.309 --> 00:13:26.949
Bulgaria and the Bulgarian people didn’t
want to change from their pagan beliefs.

00:13:26.949 --> 00:13:28.579
But Boris had a plan in mind.

00:13:28.579 --> 00:13:33.189
He quickly suppressed the rebellious populace
and then invited the exiled disciples of Cyril

00:13:33.189 --> 00:13:36.679
and Methodius which where no longer welcomed
in Moravia.

00:13:36.679 --> 00:13:40.949
He then ordered them to translate the greek
church liturgy in to old Bulgarian using the

00:13:40.949 --> 00:13:42.480
Glagolitic alphabet.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:47.230
This way Boris could expel the Greek priests
and replace them with his own Bulgarian Priests

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:49.079
all while not breaking the treaty.

00:13:49.079 --> 00:13:54.369
The clerics quickly got to work but Glagolitic
proved not ideal for old Bulgarian and so

00:13:54.369 --> 00:13:58.930
the new Cyrillic alphabet based off of the
older glagolitic was created.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:03.269
From there cyrillic quickly spread through
the Slavic orthodox lands replacing Glagolitic

00:14:03.269 --> 00:14:05.290
as the mane slavic alphabet.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:09.160
Although there were some continues remnantses
of the use of glagolitic all the way till

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.470
the 19th century mainly in Croatian church
services.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.249
The Bulgarian golden age wouldn’t however
last forever.

00:14:15.249 --> 00:14:19.179
First the Magyars arrived in the 10th century
threatening the Bulgarian borders.

00:14:19.179 --> 00:14:23.079
Second the new powerful Kievan Rus started
to take much of Bulgarian trade and influence

00:14:23.079 --> 00:14:28.439
and lastly the continues Byzantine hostilities
all culminated in the Bulgarian vasilization

00:14:28.439 --> 00:14:31.389
by the Byzantines in the early 11th century.

00:14:31.389 --> 00:14:35.019
Going back to the end of the 8th century in
the Serbo Croatian region we are starting

00:14:35.019 --> 00:14:39.259
to get more sources which is correlated with
the arrival of the Franks and Christianity

00:14:39.259 --> 00:14:40.259
in to the Region.

00:14:40.259 --> 00:14:45.569
We learn of Viseslav of Serbia the first reliable
mention of a ruler of the serbian Vlastimirovic

00:14:45.569 --> 00:14:51.209
dynasty starting in around 780 and was most
likely overseen in one way or another by the

00:14:51.209 --> 00:14:52.209
Byzantines.

00:14:52.209 --> 00:14:56.709
We also learn of Viseslav of Croatia or more
precisely Dalmacia who lived around the same

00:14:56.709 --> 00:15:00.980
time and is most well known for his early
attempts of trying to convert Dalmacia to

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:06.119
Christianity and his eventual defeat at the
hands of the franks after which Croatian Dalmacia

00:15:06.119 --> 00:15:10.100
became part of the Frankish Empire and Croatian
Panonia became a vassal.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:14.411
So at the beginning of the 9th century the
area kind of looked like this, with the slavic

00:15:14.411 --> 00:15:19.420
lands being ruled by Slavic rulers but overall
very much under the sphere of influence by

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:20.749
the two major powers.

00:15:20.749 --> 00:15:25.019
At Least until Ljudevit became the duke of
Pannonia in 810.

00:15:25.019 --> 00:15:30.019
He was raided by the Frankish duke of Friuli
and after the Emperor Louis the Pious decided

00:15:30.019 --> 00:15:34.480
not to punish the duke, enraged Ljudevit rebelled
in 819.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:38.970
He quickly started to recruit allies most
notably from the Slovenian Carantiania.

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.529
After making some initial gains the triple
armies of the Frankish king, The Duchy of

00:15:42.529 --> 00:15:47.410
Friuli and the Croatian Dalmacia which was
now ruled by Borna the successor of Viseslav

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:53.209
of Dalmacia, proved to be overwhelming for
Ljudevit who lost in 822 and escaped to the

00:15:53.209 --> 00:15:54.209
Serbian lands.

00:15:54.209 --> 00:15:59.189
He was welcomed by the successor of Viseslav
of Serbia Radoslav but Ljudevit had different

00:15:59.189 --> 00:16:00.189
plans.

00:16:00.189 --> 00:16:02.740
He killed Radoslav and tried to take control
of Serbia.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:06.720
What exactly happened after that we don’t
know but presumably it didn’t go well as

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:11.769
Ljudevit in 823 escaped to Croatian Dalmacia
now ruled by Ljudemisl.

00:16:11.769 --> 00:16:16.559
But Ljudemisl just as his predecessors Borna
was loyal to the Franks and so he promptly

00:16:16.559 --> 00:16:19.420
killed Ljudevit ending the Croatian rebelion.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:23.329
With that the Frankish rule over Croatia was
solidified and the Croatian Serbian border

00:16:23.329 --> 00:16:28.040
became the divide between the Frankish Sphere
of Influence and the Byzantine Sphere of influence.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.790
Which can be kind seen today in the division
of religion and Alphabet in the Balkans.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:37.079
Later on in Croatian Dalmacija Trpimir the
first who established the Trpimirovic dynasty

00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:41.990
that ruled croatia until 1091 would also successfully
gain autonomy by playing the Byzantine and

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:43.519
Franks off of each other.

00:16:43.519 --> 00:16:46.829
However the recognized autonomous kingdom
of Croatia wouldn’t be established until

00:16:46.829 --> 00:16:50.989
the Dalmacijan annexation of Croatian Pannonia
in 924-25.

00:16:50.989 --> 00:16:55.459
It was also during this time that the Catholic’s
church influence in the area solidified and

00:16:55.459 --> 00:16:58.170
pagan practice over all ended in Croatia.

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:02.730
In Serbia on the other hand the succession
crisis caused by Ljudevit was quickly solved

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:07.939
by Vlastimir who consolidated his power in
Serbia around the 830s but still remained

00:17:07.939 --> 00:17:09.809
under the influence of the Byzantines.

00:17:09.809 --> 00:17:14.110
He was also faced with the problem of Bulgar
advancement towards the Serbian lands but

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:18.760
against all odds defended his realm supposedly
with no Byzantine help.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:23.480
During the rest of his reign Vlastimir consolidated
his power and manage to gain Serbian independence

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.760
from the Byzantines.

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:28.230
How exactly he did that we have no written
sources about.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:33.990
After his death in the late 840s his son started
a long succession war which was won by Mutimir.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:38.810
Mutimir then went on to over see even more
successful campaigns against the Bulgars and

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:42.840
also the Christianization of the Country in
to the Eastern Orthodoxy.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:47.049
And even though there’s countless of events
I could talk about going on from here or address

00:17:47.049 --> 00:17:50.830
your comments of why I didn’t talk about
White Croatia or White Serbia which are just

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:51.830
foundation myths.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.370
I will leave it off here.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:57.710
With the Bulgars starting their golden age
and ruling over their Macedonian brothers,

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:01.024
the Serbs finally independent from the Byzantine
rule the Montenegrins partly under Byzantine

00:18:01.024 --> 00:18:02.610
and Serbian control, Croatians free from Frankish
sphere of Influence, the Bosnians probably

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:03.610
being the last slavic tribe to get Incorporated
in to the Serbo-Croatian family group and

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:06.690
Slovenians well under the German control for
a long time.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:10.510
This is not to say that all these lands were
just slavic at this point there were still

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:16.510
most likely some remnants of Roman, Illyrian,
German etc. settlements however compared to

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:21.690
the bigger political picture they were a small
spec in the Balkan Slavic Political Sphere.

